---
import Breadcrumb from "../components/Breadcrumb.astro";
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import { site } from "../config/site";
import { aboutJsonLd } from "../lib/seo";

const title = "About This US Landscaping Calculator";
const description =
  "Abdul Rauf publishes these free US calculators for gravel, mulch, topsoil, and sod. This is a personal site, not a company, with no street address or phone.";
---

<BaseLayout title={title} description={description} jsonLd={aboutJsonLd(description)}>
  <header class="page-intro">
    <Breadcrumb current="About" />
    <h1>About</h1>
  </header>
  <article class="prose">
    <h2>What is this landscaping calculator site?</h2>
    <p>
      It is a set of four free calculators that run in the browser, for common ordering questions
      about landscape material in US units. Lengths are in feet. Depth is in inches. Volume is in
      cubic feet and cubic yards. One cubic yard is 27 cubic feet. Prices, where a page asks for
      them, are in US dollars. Weight is in pounds and US short tons. A short ton is 2,000 pounds.
    </p>
    <h2>Who publishes it?</h2>
    <p>
      {site.publisherName} publishes these pages. This is a personal site, not a company.
      There is no street address, phone number, or professional credential listed here.
      The public email is {site.contact.email}, on the <a href="/contact/">Contact</a> page.
      The site does not claim a ranking or an endorsement.
    </p>
    <h2>What are the four calculators?</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><a href="/gravel-calculator/">Gravel calculator</a> for cubic yards, short tons, and bags of pea gravel, crushed stone, river rock, and a few other stones, with a density you can edit.</li>
      <li><a href="/mulch-calculator/">Mulch calculator</a> for cubic yards and for bags of 2 and 3 cubic feet, with a 2 to 4 inch depth guide for beds and trees.</li>
      <li><a href="/topsoil-calculator/">Topsoil calculator</a> for cubic yards, short tons, and bags of screened topsoil, garden mix, or fill dirt.</li>
      <li><a href="/sod-calculator/">Sod calculator</a> for square feet, pallets, and rolls, using a pallet size and roll size you can change to match the farm.</li>
    </ul>
    <h2>How are the numbers handled?</h2>
    <p>
      Each result includes the working, in the same order as the arithmetic. The
      <a href="/methodology/">methodology</a> lists the formulas and the density behind every
      preset, with the reference it came from. A preset is a planning figure. The number on a
      supplier ticket replaces it.
    </p>
    <p>
      None of the calculators chooses a driveway section, a drainage layout, or a planting plan.
      Those decisions stay with you, your supplier, or a qualified professional. The
      <a href="/disclaimer/">disclaimer</a> states that limit for all four pages.
    </p>
    <p>Last updated {site.updatedLabel}.</p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
